# The PJ is shared between a Mac and a Windows PC through Google Drive (decision 2026-11-12).
# Default: byte-exact, never converted. Recorded inputs and results (json / jsonl / csv / log / SEED ...) keep the bytes
# whose sha256 are written in data.md / env.md / notes; some outputs made on Windows on 2026-11-11 are CRLF on purpose
# (dry-run decisions 判断 9). This also stops Windows' core.autocrlf=true from rewriting any file on checkout.
*           -text
*.parquet   binary

# Sources: always LF in the repo and in the working tree, so the Mac and Colab never get CRLF shell / Python files.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.lock      text eol=lf
*.ipynb     text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
.gitignore  text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Exception: an experiment record committed as CRLF (part of the 2026-11-11 llm-dry-run record). Keep its bytes; do
# not renormalize.
experiments/20261111-llm-dry-run/run_colab.ipynb -text
